{"base":"7feb0188ec550135e70f4f16a4ab7051095077b2","description":"Converge writes on duplicate releases per OID\n\n- replace the ambiguity error in find_or_create_by_oid\n  with a deterministic tie-break on the smallest\n  ReleaseId: `rad-artifact add` was unusable whenever\n  two nodes had concurrently created a release for the\n  same commit before syncing\n- drop FindOrCreateError and return store::Error\n  directly: without the Ambiguous variant the wrapper\n  no longer carries its weight\n- simplify add_artifact error mapping accordingly\n- rewrite the ambiguity test to assert that duplicate\n  release COBs converge on the same canonical id across\n  signers, so new artifacts pile onto one release\n  rather than spawning more duplicates; the read path\n  (find_all_by_cid) still unions artifacts across\n  duplicates for retrieval\n\n\ncli: add location to one release in serve cmd\n\n- Register the iroh:// serve location on only the latest release\n  containing the CID instead of every matching release. Fetchers\n  already union locations across all releases containing the CID, so\n  replicating the registration was redundant write amplification.\n- Clean up the matching remove_location path so shutdown retracts the\n  single location we added rather than looping.\n- Drop the single-result find_by_cid and rename find_all_by_cid to\n  find_by_cid so the remaining API reflects the one real use case —\n  aggregating every release that carries a CID so callers can union\n  locations across duplicates.\n\nWhy: the previous fan-out was based on a backwards reading of the\nfetcher's union behavior — since fetch aggregates across releases, one\nregistration suffices and we avoid spurious COB writes when the same\nCID appears in many releases.\n\n\nRefine release pretty print output","oid":"69e1b20c50ae67ef7400b4597ce6b237af143bf3","type":"revision"}